{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/635461-beast-possible-z-splat","id":635461,"title":"[Beast] Possible Z-Splat?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-08-21T23:16:07-07:00","id":635461,"title":"[Beast] Possible Z-Splat?","content":"I know that Beast was not written like typical nWoD game. And that original &quot;Z-Splat&quot; is probably the Horror itself for characters. But if you would need to make one, what would it be?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-21T23:20:24-07:00","id":635475,"title":"","content":"Probably something based on Families, going into more specific nightmares. &quot;I am the terror that flaps in the night! I am the weirdo who sits next to you on the bus!&quot;, that sort of thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-22T06:50:59-07:00","id":635727,"title":"","content":"I would actually go with a Legacy style z-splat. And, by Legacy style, I mean base it on either Hunger or Family as necessary, or maybe both. I can see a Medusa sub-faction, and I can see a dragon-like Collector. Actually, I'd say the biggest requirement would be <i>Legend</i>, the virtue/vice equivalent thing. The z-splat is all about the Legend you build.<br /> <br /> It would come with a permanent Athanama as well. The dragon-like Collectors would pick up the one where you obsessively kidnap people, <br /> <br /> The benefits? I would actually put in the form of expanded Lairs and Horror-form when you merge / open primordial pathway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-22T08:07:30-07:00","id":635815,"title":"","content":"I'd wondered about adding a &quot;factional&quot; splat - while Hunger can change, it's not something that happens often or easily, and isn't really chosen - it's more like two X-splats than an X and Y. Which is interesting, but I'd thought about a Y.<br /> <br /> <b>Preachers:</b> These are the ones that take the teaching-through-fear aspect of the second draft to heart. How they teach may coincide with how they feed, or the two may be orthogonal. Either way, while they take what they need from humans, they see themselves - sincerely, wishfully, or hypocritically as the case may be - serving humanity as a whole. At their worst that's an excuse for their abuses, while at their best it's a reason for them to hunt down Beasts who prey wantonly.<br /> <br /> <b>Isolates:</b> One thing I like about Beast, especially the first draft, is its potential for Beasts to engage with the world much as mortals do - they frequently feed via normal-seeming activites, they don't have a society that imposes a supernatural life on them to replace their human one. So Isolates are the Beasts who go that route - their lives mostly parallel their former human ones - even if they have extra concerns with their Hungers and the hidden world around them. In this, they can be as good and bad as humans are.<br /> <br /> <b>Revelers:</b> &quot;The Predator must hunt. The Collector must take. The Tyrant must rule. These are not cravings; they are categorical imperatives.&quot; That's the heart of the Revellers. Feeding their Horrors is simply <i>right</i>. Revelers feed without guilt or shame, though not necessarily without conscience: while feeding may be right, that doesn't mean a Beast won't ever try to balance that with other things she thinks are right.<br /> <br /> <b>Mediators:</b> The Mediators are the ones who take matters of family and extended family most to heart. They seek out other supernaturals, and use their kinship abilities to build themselves a place as ambassadors, messengers, and diplomats - getting on with your cousins is good, but helping them get on with each other is even better. More selfishly, it's a route to power, because opportunities to form kinship ties are plentiful.<br /> <br /> [I'd want a fifth of course]<br /> <br /> <br /> For a proper Z, I'd go with what <b>MCN</b> suggested, except I'd make it <i>explicitly</i> based on both: your Z* comes from a specific intersection of your Family and Hunger. One effect would be to lock in your Hunger permanently, so it can't change even under the rare circumstances it otherwise might.<br /> <br /> * Maybe call it Anima, Ador, or Genius.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-02T13:46:48-07:00","id":649277,"title":"","content":"The Z-splat could be some dark mirrors of Heroes, who instead of hating Beasts are awed by them, or who try to appease them rather than fight them.<br /> They'd be the guys who lead the unwary travellers into the haunted forest, or offer the princess as a sacrifice to the dragon. They'd benefit socially or metaphysically from the Beast's depredation and would try to create a system to have them continue.<br /> <br /> Or they could be people bonded to deffective or nascent Horrors who don't have Lairs of their own, and none of the power that comes with it. They'd be scavengers to the Beast's predators, feeding on scraps of the Beasts' meals.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-02T14:12:39-07:00","id":649298,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/635461-beast-possible-z-splat?p=649277#post649277\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Z-splat could be some dark mirrors of Heroes, who instead of hating Beasts are awed by them, or who try to appease them rather than fight them.<br /> They'd be the guys who lead the unwary travellers into the haunted forest, or offer the princess as a sacrifice to the dragon. They'd benefit socially or metaphysically from the Beast's depredation and would try to create a system to have them continue.<br /> <br /> Or they could be people bonded to deffective or nascent Horrors who don't have Lairs of their own, and none of the power that comes with it. They'd be scavengers to the Beast's predators, feeding on scraps of the Beasts' meals.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I think you've fundamentally misunderstood what a Z-splat is.<br /> <br /> The lettered pattern starts at X-splat for the inborn and unchangeable aspect of your template, goes on to Y-splat for the social/philosophical axis of the splat as a whole that your character identifies themself by, and stops at Z-splat, which is typically an overtly optional degree of further specialization like bloodlines or lodges or Legacies or entitlements.<br /> <br /> You're describing a demisplat or a B-splat, which is a wholly separate category of entity that you don't specialize <i>into</i> if it has any causal relationship with the main/A-splat whose name is in the game title.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-02T16:14:47-07:00","id":649501,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/635461-beast-possible-z-splat?p=649298#post649298\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think you've fundamentally misunderstood what a Z-splat is.<br /> <br /> The lettered pattern starts at X-splat for the inborn and unchangeable aspect of your template, goes on to Y-splat for the social/philosophical axis of the splat as a whole that your character identifies themself by, and stops at Z-splat, which is typically an overtly optional degree of further specialization like bloodlines or lodges or Legacies or entitlements.<br /> <br /> You're describing a demisplat or a B-splat, which is a wholly separate category of entity that you don't specialize <i>into</i> if it has any causal relationship with the main/A-splat whose name is in the game title.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, I was indeed mstaaken thanks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-02T16:15:48-07:00","id":649504,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/635461-beast-possible-z-splat?p=635815#post635815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd wondered about adding a &quot;factional&quot; splat - while Hunger can change, it's not something that happens often or easily, and isn't really chosen - it's more like two X-splats than an X and Y. Which is interesting, but I'd thought about a Y.<br /> <br /> <b>Preachers:</b> These are the ones that take the teaching-through-fear aspect of the second draft to heart. How they teach may coincide with how they feed, or the two may be orthogonal. Either way, while they take what they need from humans, they see themselves - sincerely, wishfully, or hypocritically as the case may be - serving humanity as a whole. At their worst that's an excuse for their abuses, while at their best it's a reason for them to hunt down Beasts who prey wantonly.<br /> <br /> <b>Isolates:</b> One thing I like about Beast, especially the first draft, is its potential for Beasts to engage with the world much as mortals do - they frequently feed via normal-seeming activites, they don't have a society that imposes a supernatural life on them to replace their human one. So Isolates are the Beasts who go that route - their lives mostly parallel their former human ones - even if they have extra concerns with their Hungers and the hidden world around them. In this, they can be as good and bad as humans are.<br /> <br /> <b>Revelers:</b> &quot;The Predator must hunt. The Collector must take. The Tyrant must rule. These are not cravings; they are categorical imperatives.&quot; That's the heart of the Revellers. Feeding their Horrors is simply <i>right</i>. Revelers feed without guilt or shame, though not necessarily without conscience: while feeding may be right, that doesn't mean a Beast won't ever try to balance that with other things she thinks are right.<br /> <br /> <b>Mediators:</b> The Mediators are the ones who take matters of family and extended family most to heart. They seek out other supernaturals, and use their kinship abilities to build themselves a place as ambassadors, messengers, and diplomats - getting on with your cousins is good, but helping them get on with each other is even better. More selfishly, it's a route to power, because opportunities to form kinship ties are plentiful.<br /> <br /> [I'd want a fifth of course]<br /> <br /> For a proper Z, I'd go with what <b>MCN</b> suggested, except I'd make it <i>explicitly</i> based on both: your Z* comes from a specific intersection of your Family and Hunger. One effect would be to lock in your Hunger permanently, so it can't change even under the rare circumstances it otherwise might.<br /> <br /> * Maybe call it Anima, Ador, or Genius.</div> </div> </div> </div> I like that a whole lot! I think such a Z splat would be a big intersection of Family, Hunger, Philosophical Faction, Legend and Kinships. Perhaps we could take cues from <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/569722-optional-rules-for-beast-clade\"><b>this thread</b></a>, which also proposes a type of Z splat. I'm tempted to call it Mythos, as a reference to both Lovecraft and the <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Franchise/TheFearMythos?from=Main.TheFearMythos\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Fear Mythos</b></a>.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{