lace their human one. So Isolates are the Beasts who go that route - their lives mostly parallel their former human ones - even if they have extra concerns with their Hungers and the hidden world around them. In this, they can be as good and bad as humans are.<br /> <br /> <b>Revelers:</b> &quot;The Predator must hunt. The Collector must take. The Tyrant must rule. These are not cravings; they are categorical imperatives.&quot; That's the heart of the Revellers. Feeding their Horrors is simply <i>right</i>. Revelers feed without guilt or shame, though not necessarily without conscience: while feeding may be right, that doesn't mean a Beast won't ever try to balance that with other things she thinks are right.<br /> <br /> <b>Mediators:</b> The Mediators are the ones who take matters of family and extended family most to heart. They seek out other supernaturals, and use their kinship abilities to build themselves a place as ambassadors, messengers, and diplomats - getting on with your cousins is good, but helping them get on with each other is even better. More selfishly, it's a route to power, because opportunities to form kinship ties are plentiful.<br /> <br /> [I'd want a fifth of course]<br /> <br /> <br /> For a proper Z, I'd go with what <b>MCN</b> suggested, except I'd make it <i>explicitly</i> based on both: your Z* comes from a specific intersection of your Family and Hunger. One effect would be to lock in your Hunger permanently, so it can't change even under the rare circumstances it otherwise might.<br /> <br /> * Maybe call it Anima, Ador, or Genius.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Have you by chance Expanded on this Concept, I like the factional aspect as opposed to adding a forced Z splat because &quot;all other lines have one&quot;, I am also working on a character concept that is pretty spot on for an isolate, being by his nature an aloof and private Makara, forced to deal with and come to terms with the young Beasts(the PCs) moving into his city.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Keep your Friends Close and your Enemies at Knife point.","edited":{"userid":10265,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10265-neksys","user":"Neksys","date":". 12-15-2015, 01:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10265-neksys","name":"Neksys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10265_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-15T10:21:13-08:00","id":786784,"title":"","content":"How about a z-splat based around becoming more like a different supernatural creature? Like the Beast gains some of their strength in the form of unique Atavisms, but also gains a permanent Anathema that's thematically appropriate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/477-xenorath","name":"Xenorath","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"169"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-15T17:43:50-08:00","id":787055,"title":"","content":"I do kinda like that. Use the z-splat to expand on Family themes and mechanics, although they're pretty thorough as is","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-24T09:32:17-08:00","id":792225,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/635461-beast-possible-z-splat?p=635815#post635815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd wondered about adding a &quot;factional&quot; splat - while Hunger can change, it's not something that happens often or easily, and isn't really chosen - it's more like two X-splats than an X and Y. Which is interesting, but I'd thought about a Y.<br /> <br /> [...]<br /> <br /> [I'd want a fifth of course]</div> </div> </div> </div>Denialists. Seekers of internal balance who take minimally and give back to the community they take from, and seek a Golconda-equivalent where they do not need to feed violently anymore.<br /> <br /> One of the few Beast factions to interact mutually favourably with Dreamspeakers.<br /> <br /> Potential nicknames: Vegans, Autotrophes","signature":"","edited":{"userid":10091,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10091-altasaire","user":"Altasaire","date":". 12-24-2015, 12:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10091-altasaire","name":"Altasaire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10091_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-31T05:39:37-08:00","id":797292,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Altasaire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/635461-beast-possible-z-splat?p=792225#post792225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Denialists. Seekers of internal balance who take minimally and give back to the community they take from, and seek a Golconda-equivalent where they do not need to feed violently anymore.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neksys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/635461-beast-possible-z-splat?p=786523#post786523\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have you by chance Expanded on this Concept, I like the factional aspect as opposed to adding a forced Z splat because &quot;all other lines have one&quot;, I am also working on a character concept that is pretty spot on for an isolate, being by his nature an aloof and private Makara, forced to deal with and come to terms with the young Beasts(the PCs) moving into his city.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not yet. I doubt I'll put in much more thought till the game itself is out.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"tha